Cyde Weys wrote:

> Any last suggestions before I do this thing?  I have three wishes on the 
> WoW to use before I go up ... any ideas?

Name the real amulet, but make sure it's real by trying to put it in a 
bag first. It'll save you some hassle.

Bless the things you haven't yet, especially anything you're wearing. 
You never know when you'll need to take those lenses off and put on a 
blindfold. Use that ring of conflict + Elbereth frequently, and just sit 
there. It'll help clear the levels quickly (esp. on air and fire, where 
most creatures have line of sight to you).

You may want to bring your +4 armor down to +3 and reenchant it, hoping 
for +5. I personally recommend keeping your wand of death OUTSIDE the 
pack, but you need to remember to stash it quick if you meet an energy 
beast. You don't really need to wear your slow digest ring anymore 
unless you're doing a lot of sitting around (which is just asking for 
the Wiz).

For wishes you may want a blessed figurine of a ki-rin and a saddle, 
they make excellent steeds. Save a wish for a cockatrice corpse for the 
astral plane unless you've already geno'd them. A helm of opposite 
alignment will do you good if the first altar you check out is Lawful.

The gems are probably not worth the weight.

